WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.060
With Black Lightning, DC launched its first
television show starring a black superhero.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.200
It's a milestone that's been a long time coming,
but it's not the first time Jefferson Pierce

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.990
has managed to break a long-standing barrier:
since first appearing over 40 years ago, he’s

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.090
served as a member of the Justice League,
the Outsiders, a solo superhero, and even

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.700
provided the DC Universe with a legacy of
heroic characters.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.580
From his origins on the page all the way to
his current status on the screen, here's the

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.760
fascinating truth behind Black Lightning.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.240
DC's First Black Superhero

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:35.060
The first three decades of the superhero genre
were overwhelmingly white, but in the late

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.460
'60s, that began to change.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:42.520
At Marvel, Stan Lee and Jack Kirby introduced
the Black Panther, and in 1973, Hero For Hire

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.940
#1 made Luke Cage the first black superhero
to headline his own book.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.940
At DC, however, things moved a little more
slowly.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:55.120
It wasn’t until 1977 that Tony Isabella,
a writer who had previously worked on Luke

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.820
Cage's adventures, was hired to create their
first headlining black superhero.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.540
With Isabella and artist Trevor von Eeden,
that year saw the debut of Black Lightning.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.360
Jefferson Pierce was a Gold Medal-winning
Olympic decathlete who returned to his old

00:01:07.369 --> 00:01:09.880
neighborhood in Metropolis to work as a teacher.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.350
When one of his students was killed in an
altercation with the a criminal organization

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:17.390
called the 100, Pierce decided to hit the
streets with a high-tech costume to take them

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.080
on himself.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.820
The Black Bomber, the hero that almost was

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.200
While Black Lightning was the idea that made
it to the page, he wasn’t DC’s first thought

00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:29.679
when it came to creating a black superhero
— and as Isabella revealed on his blog,

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.060
the original plan might’ve been the worst
idea in comics history.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.100
When Isabella was hired, the editors pitched
him a character called the Black Bomber, with

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.759
the hook being that he was actually a white
racist who turned into a super-powered black

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:44.900
man when he was stressed out, with neither
personality being aware of the other.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.500
In other words, DC's first black superhero
was not actually going to be black, and would

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.320
feature plenty of stereotypes including a
basketball uniform costume.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.760
Fortunately for everyone concerned, Isabella
talked them out of it.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:01.060
Thirty years later, though, writer Dwayne
McDuffie, well known for making satirical

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.770
jabs at the superhero genre, worked him into
a story about an alternate reality where everything

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:09.120
had gone so wrong that the Brown Bomber could
be on the Justice League.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:11.040
The Outsiders

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:16.180
The original run of Black Lightning was canceled
after only 11 issues, but if it's any consolation,

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:17.200
it wasn't alone.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.080
Instead, it was a casualty of what fans have
dubbed the DC Implosion.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:24.299
All told, DC gave the axe to 20 titles.

00:02:24.299 --> 00:02:28.460
It was a move that came so suddenly that most
of those series even had completely finished

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.870
stories, including Black Lightning #12, that
stayed in DC's archives until they were published

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.440
in a book called Cancelled Comic Cavalcade
to secure the copyrights.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.880
Five years later, Black Lightning got a second
chance at stardom.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:44.989
When Batman quit the Justice League over that
team's reluctance to cause an international

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:48.099
incident, he put together a new team called
the Outsiders.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:52.170
The roster included a handful of new characters
like Katana, who would go on to appear in

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.860
the Suicide Squad movie, but it also revived
a few existing heroes, including Black Lightning.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:00.780
Over the course of the Outsiders' five-year
run, everyone on the team got a spotlight

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.980
story highlighting their mysterious and/or
tortured past, and Black Lightning was no

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:05.480
exception.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:10.180
In his case, he'd given up his costumed identity
and powers due to guilt over the accidental

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.740
death of a bystander named Trina Shelton,
whose family would eventually return to get

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:15.240
revenge.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.040
I'm the one who taught him to fly!

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.580
Black Lightning headlining his own show is
a new development, but Cress Williams isn't

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.420
actually the first actor to ever play the
character in live action.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.769
That honor, believe it or not, goes to stand-up
comedian Sinbad, who took a brief turn as

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:32.040
Black Lightning on a 1992 episode of Saturday
Night Live.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:36.960
In a sketch set at Superman's funeral, tying
into the then-current Death of Superman storyline,

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.900
cast members like Chris Farley, Dana Carvey,
and Chris Rock appeared as Superman's fellow

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.400
heroes.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:46.880
However, Black Lightning wasn't invited, leading
to an altercation with Jimmy Olsen.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.120
And… by the way - SNL effects department
- that's not what lightning looks like.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:54.640
It's not the most flattering portrayal for
sure —and the part where Batman doesn't

00:03:54.659 --> 00:03:58.790
recognize his old teammate is a real heartbreaker
— but it is an interesting bit of pop cultural

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:02.500
prominence for a character who was still pretty
obscure for mainstream audiences.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.500
Thunder, Lightning, and Grace

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.260
With Black Lightning's ties to the original
roster of the Outsiders, it's not surprising

00:04:09.269 --> 00:04:13.560
that he'd have a connection to the team when
a new version was put together in 2003.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:18.811
In Outsiders #1, Judd Winick and Tom Raney
introduced Anissa Pierce, AKA Thunder, the

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.800
oldest of Black Lightning's two daughters.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.720
Like her father, Anissa added some much-needed
diversity to the DC Universe when it was revealed

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.920
that she was in a romantic relationship with
another member of the outsiders, Grace Choi.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.380
Her powers, however, are completely different.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.780
She can control her density, making her nearly
invulnerable.

00:04:34.781 --> 00:04:40.440
In 2008, Anissa’s younger sister Jennifer
— originally introduced as part of another

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.960
alternate reality in the pages of Kingdom
Come — joined her in the mainstream continuity.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.280
With powers that were similar to her father’s,
she took the name “Lightning.”

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.160
Joining the Justice League

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.980
In 1979, Black Lightning was offered membership
in the JLA, but turned it down, becoming only

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.090
the second character ever to do so.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:00.300
30 years later, he finally accepted.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:05.350
In 2006, Batman, Superman, and Wonder Woman
spent a story arc literally sitting around

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:09.280
a table with a bunch of trading card-style
photographs of their fellow heroes, debating

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.400
who they should let into a reformed League.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.940
Around that same time, a swamp zombie rebuilt
a killer robot so he could turn Red Tornado

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.980
human and then tear off his arm and eat it.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:21.480
Yeah, that really happened… but anyway that
was the McGuffin to get Black Lightning, and

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.620
the rest, to join up.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:26.740
The Justice League decided to just keep everyone
who showed up to fight the latest crisis,

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.070
and he stuck around for the next few years.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:34.260
After DC rebooted their universe in 2011,
and then "rebirthed" it in 2016, he was out

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.440
of the League and back to being a solo hero.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.680
The CW's Black Lightning

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.580
With the new Black Lightning TV show, the
CW is pulling from the entire history of the

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.560
character in some pretty interesting ways.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:50.080
Cress Williams stars as Jefferson Pierce,
who still works in education in his TV incarnation.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:54.580
He's the principal of a high school in the
city of Freeland who has dedicated his tenure

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.780
to helping kids and eliminating violence.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:01.420
Like his earliest comics incarnation, the
CW's Black Lightning is taking on the 100

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.100
and Tobias Whale, and getting his costume
and equipment from Peter Gambi.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:09.260
Like the version that showed up in Batman
and the Outsiders, he's been retired from

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:13.380
superheroics, driven to give up on being a
vigilante by his aversion to violence.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.220
Anissa and Jennifer have already appeared
on the show, both with the powers they have

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:20.280
the comics, and Grace Choi is there as Anissa’s
love interest.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:23.900
The only thing that could really complete
the saga is if they managed to get an appearance

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:24.660
by Sinbad.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:25.900
Thanks for watching!

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.700
